    "###  Answer\n",
    "\n",
    "Parity measures whether the two qubits agree. Outcomes `00` and `11` have parity **+1**; outcomes `01` and `10` have parity **−1**. Therefore\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\\langle P \\rangle = (P_{00}+P_{11}) - (P_{01}+P_{10}).$$\n",
    "\n",
    "In the Z basis we use the counts measured directly. For the X basis, we apply H to both qubits before measuring and use those counts. The value ranges from −1 (always anticorrelated) through 0 (no correlation) to +1 (always correlated)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 12,
   "id": "a1e5c0d2",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "state      basis    sampled   exact\n",
      "Bell-plus  Z         +1.000  +1.000\n",
      "Bell-plus  X         +1.000  +1.000\n",
      "Bell-minus Z         +1.000  +1.000\n",
      "Bell-minus X         -1.000  -1.000\n",
      "\n",
      "Product state (H on both qubits): Z parity = +0.000, X parity = +1.000\n",
      "Self-check passed.\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "def parity_expectation(counts: dict) -> float:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Return (P00+P11) − (P01+P10) estimated from two-qubit counts.\"\"\"\n",
    "    shots = sum(counts.values())\n",
    "    even = counts.get(\"00\", 0) + counts.get(\"11\", 0)\n",
    "    odd = counts.get(\"01\", 0) + counts.get(\"10\", 0)\n",
    "    return (even - odd) / shots\n",
    "\n",
    "def exact_parity(circuit: QuantumCircuit, basis: str = \"Z\") -> float:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Exact parity from the statevector (no shot noise), for comparison.\"\"\"\n",
    "    qc = circuit.copy()\n",
    "    if basis == \"X\":\n",
    "        qc.h([0, 1])\n",
    "    p = Statevector.from_instruction(qc).probabilities_dict()\n",
    "    return (p.get(\"00\", 0) + p.get(\"11\", 0)) - (p.get(\"01\", 0) + p.get(\"10\", 0))\n",
    "\n",
    "states = {\"plus\": bell_plus(), \"minus\": bell_minus()}\n",
    "parities = {}\n",
    "print(f\"{'state':<11}{'basis':<7}{'sampled':>9}{'exact':>8}\")\n",
    "for kind, circuit in states.items():\n",
    "    for basis in (\"Z\", \"X\"):\n",
    "        sampled = parity_expectation(bell_counts(kind, basis))\n",
    "        exact = exact_parity(circuit, basis)\n",
    "        parities[(kind, basis)] = sampled\n",
    "        print(f\"Bell-{kind:<6}{basis:<7}{sampled:>+9.3f}{exact:>+8.3f}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "product_parity = {b: exact_parity(product, b) for b in (\"Z\", \"X\")}\n",
    "print(f\"\\nProduct state (H on both qubits): Z parity = {product_parity['Z']:+.3f}, X parity = {product_parity['X']:+.3f}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Visible self-check: signs should be +, +, +, − for the Bell states\n",
    "assert parities[(\"plus\", \"Z\")] > 0.9 and parities[(\"plus\", \"X\")] > 0.9\n",
    "assert parities[(\"minus\", \"Z\")] > 0.9 and parities[(\"minus\", \"X\")] < -0.9\n",
    "print(\"Self-check passed.\")"
   ]
  },
